      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The FDA labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. This order is about double the maximum, even though the patient has normal kidney and liver function. Common error patterns here include confusing mg with mL or a misplaced decimal, or mixing up the per-dose and daily totals.\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. For example:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- Or, if the 1700 mg figure is correct, tell me the formulation and the reason for the dose, and I can enter it with a note.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
